# Disk geometries in the cpmtools syntax. Besides its own keys:
#   sides int|seq   - how the image orders the sides (int: both sides of a cylinder in turn)
#   charmap         - the character set the viewer starts on
#   layout          - how a controller lays the sectors down on a whole track, for the
#                     formats that keep the bit cells (HFE): ibm-mfm (System/34 MFM),
#                     ibm-fm (IBM 3740 FM, 8") or dvk-mx (the DVK MX track)
#   bitrate, rpm    - data rate in kbit/s and the speed of the drive; 250 kbit/s (125 for
#                     dvk-mx) and 300 rpm (360 for ibm-fm) when not given
#   gap4a, gap1, gap2, gap3, indexmark
#                   - the gaps of an IBM track and whether it starts with the index mark
#                     (C2 C2 C2 FC / FC); the IBM values fitted to the turn when not given

diskdef korvet
  seclen 1024
  heads 2
  tracks 80
  sectrk 5
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 128
  boottrk 1
  layout ibm-mfm
end

