# Apple 3.5" 800 Kb, 1600 ProDOS blocks. A .po image is a plain sequence of blocks,
# while the disk itself is zoned (8 to 12 sectors per track), so the geometry below
# is nominal and only serves to address the blocks in order.
diskdef prodos-800
  seclen 512
  heads 1
  tracks 160
  sectrk 10
end

# RT-11 disks of the DVK, BK and UKNC. RT-11 sees a volume as a run of 512 byte blocks;
# the images keep the sectors in order, both sides of a cylinder in turn.
# DX (RX01, 8"): 77 tracks of 26 sectors of 128 bytes in physical order. The RT-11
# interleave and the unused track 0 are applied by the filesystem itself.
diskdef dx
  seclen 128
  heads 1
  tracks 77
  sectrk 26
  layout ibm-fm
end

